#!RuleTest
#test CT-RUN-1 expect=noViolation domain=VS
#note Fold F1 / F4 pin of TODAY's output — a TIG SDTM-leg run is UNKNOWN-kind (standard "tig"), which the store never serves (P0), so it consumes no CT root and never reads a Trial Summary. Its 2.1 define declares sdtmct-2024-09-27: the selection stays DEFINE (step 4) exactly as today, with no TS note; with no store serving it the rule finds no library codelist and does not fire. The TS names sdtmct-1999-01-01: a wrongful TS read would replace the define's set and the note would say so.
#run-product tig/1-0/sdtm
#define-xml define-21-sdtm-2024-09-27.xml
#ct-available none
dataset VS
col VSSTAT type=Char
---
BOGUS
---

dataset TS
col STUDYID  type=Char
col TSPARMCD type=Char
col TSVAL    type=Char
col TSVCDREF type=Char
col TSVCDVER type=Char
---
S1 | TCNTRL | PLACEBO | CDISC CT | 1999-01-01
---
